  "answer": "To reduce the risk of language models producing toxic content such as hate speech, insults, profanity, and threats, researchers have proposed combining data filtering, output filtering, and steering (https://www.deepmind.com/blog/challenges-in-detoxifying-language-models). The implementation mechanisms include filtering the pre-training data by removing or down-weighting texts that receive a high toxicity score from tools like the Perspective API, and applying output filtering during the decoding process by using a fine-tuned BERT toxicity classifier to score candidate continuations and reject those that are toxic (https://www.deepmind.com/blog/challenges-in-detoxifying-language-models)."
